<title>USA: U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture said Monday that 93 percent of the U.S. corn crop had been harvested, compared to 88 percent a week ago and a five-year average of 92 percent.</p>
<p>In its report on Nov. 24 conditions, USDA said 94 percent of the soybean crop was harvested. A week earlier, 92 percent had been harvested, and the five-year average is 97 percent.</p>
<p>USDA said 82 percent of the cotton crop was harvested versus 77 percent last week, and 82 percent average.</p>
<p>The department also reported 3 percent of the winter wheat crop was in poor condition, 23 percent fair, 63 percent good and 11 percent excellent.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
</text>
